course: dictionary
lesson: 10690
title: Unrelated: no link between things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unrelated means there is no link or connection between two things. Look at the words around it to find out what is not linked. «Hand, foot and mouth disease is a mild childhood virus with mouth ulcers and spots on the hands and feet, unrelated to the cattle disease.» The two diseases might sound alike, but the sentence says they have no link.
explain: Unrelated can also mean two people are not in the same family. Two animals can be unrelated even when they look alike or do the same thing. «A giraffe has 7 neck bones and a sauropod had 12 to 19; unrelated animals finding the same answer to reaching high food is called convergence.» These animals are not family, yet they found a similar answer.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If «the two diseases have no link» still makes sense, unrelated is the right word for it.
fact: Unrelated means having no link or connection with each other.
fact: Unrelated people are not part of the same family.
fact: In science and maths, unrelated facts or numbers do not affect each other.
fact: «Unrelated» animals can find the same answer to a problem, such as reaching high food; this is called convergence.
fact: In the wild, the leaders of a wolf pack are simply the parents, not unrelated wolves who fight to be boss.
exercise: «Hand, foot and mouth disease is a mild childhood virus, unrelated to the cattle disease.» What does unrelated mean here? | Strangers who look alike | *No link or connection between the two diseases | Very serious and dangerous | Both caught from cattle
exercise: Ruby says, «On an unrelated note, let's talk about my new bike.» What does unrelated tell you? | *The talk is changing to a different topic | Ruby is making a list of notes | The talk is about the same thing as before | The bike is broken
exercise: «Unrelated animals finding the same answer to reaching high food is called convergence.» Find and copy one word that means not family. | animals | *unrelated | convergence | finding
test: «A giraffe has 7 neck bones and a sauropod had 12 to 19.» Why does this show the animals are unrelated? | They both have seven neck bones | They both eat high leaves on purpose | *They are not part of the same family | They are the same kind of animal
test: Nadia says, «Unrelated means the same as related.» Is she right? | *No, unrelated means there is no link between two things | No, unrelated means very big | Yes, but only for animals | Yes, they mean the same
exam: «The alpha wolf idea came from unrelated wolves kept together in zoos.» What does unrelated tell us about these wolves? | They were all from the same family | They were the same colour as each other | *They were not family and had no close link | They were the parents of the pack
